<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18665" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fossūra</span></b> , ae, f.
		fodio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a digging</i> (postAug., whereas fossio is quite class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plana fossura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 14, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Pall. 10, 14, 2</span></i>.—In
				plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">complanata juga fossuris montium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puteorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					5, 9, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 28, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, concr., <i>a pit</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">summa fossura operiatur arundinibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					8, 1, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
